{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"fa362c9c4d375461","name":"card_event_lightning_strike","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Germany/Breakthrough/events/card_event_lightning_strike","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"LIGHTNING STRIKE","text":"When the enemy draws an extra card, deal 4 damage to the enemy HQ.","flavorText":"The Battle of Britain began in 1940 and the Germans started with air attacks on British shipping, ports and military installations. Luftwaffe’s aim was to destroy RAF, which they came close to doing several times in the summer of 1940, not least when they attacked the visible and vital radar masts at key airfields. Hitler had ordered that London should not be bombed except on his orders, but due to a mistake bombs were dropped on the capital. In retaliation the British bombed Berlin and from then on the Luftwaffe started daily raids on British cities. The Blitz had started. Some historians argue that this change in strategy turned the tides in the Battle of Britain, the attacks on airfields halted and this gave RAF the breathing space it needed to establish air superiority over Britain.","faction":"Germany","type":"gotcha","rarity":"Uncommon","cost":1,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_lightning_strike","title":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_event_lightning_strike_title","SourceString":"LIGHTNING STRIKE","LocalizedString":"LIGHTNING STRIKE"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::gotcha","faction":"EFactionEnum::Germany","kredits":1,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_event_lightning_strike_text","SourceString":"When the enemy draws an extra card, deal 4 damage to the enemy HQ.","LocalizedString":"When the enemy draws an extra card, deal 4 damage to the enemy HQ."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_event_lightning_strike_history","SourceString":"The Battle of Britain began in 1940 and the Germans started with air attacks on British shipping, ports and military installations. Luftwaffe’s aim was to destroy RAF, which they came close to doing several times in the summer of 1940, not least when they attacked the visible and vital radar masts at key airfields. Hitler had ordered that London should not be bombed except on his orders, but due to a mistake bombs were dropped on the capital. In retaliation the British bombed Berlin and from then on the Luftwaffe started daily raids on British cities. The Blitz had started. Some historians argue that this change in strategy turned the tides in the Battle of Britain, the attacks on airfields halted and this gave RAF the breathing space it needed to establish air superiority over Britain.","LocalizedString":"The Battle of Britain began in 1940 and the Germans started with air attacks on British shipping, ports and military installations. Luftwaffe’s aim was to destroy RAF, which they came close to doing several times in the summer of 1940, not least when they attacked the visible and vital radar masts at key airfields. Hitler had ordered that London should not be bombed except on his orders, but due to a mistake bombs were dropped on the capital. In retaliation the British bombed Berlin and from then on the Luftwaffe started daily raids on British cities. The Blitz had started. Some historians argue that this change in strategy turned the tides in the Battle of Britain, the attacks on airfields halted and this gave RAF the breathing space it needed to establish air superiority over Britain."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Uncommon","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Breakthrough","returnSet":"ECardSetEnum::CurrentExpansion","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardDrawnFromDeck"],"soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'War_UI_Class_Specific_Engineer_Socket_Crank_Sequence_2'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/War_UI/Waves/Class_Specific/War_UI_Class_Specific_Engineer_Socket_Crank_Sequence_2.0"},"soundAttack":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'Anihilation_17'","ObjectPath":"kards/Conten